  {
    "sha": "3c4bb5c11a4502e430e78d9cab40f693783766fe",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVmlK7doAKDNjNGJiNWMxMWE0NTAyZTQzMGU3OGQ5Y2FiNDBmNjkzNzgzNzY2ZmU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-08T00:00:50Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-08T00:00:50Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): a fresh depth operation bottoms out at the part's floor, not the G54 plane\n\nA new 2D Contour (and every depth kind seeded from the default Face) took\nits bottom from Carried::of's fallback, WorkOffset(0)+0 - the G54 Z0\nplane. With G54 Z zeroed on the part's top, a common shop habit, that\nbottom resolved level with the top (TopOfModel+0), and CreateOperation\nrefused the zero-depth operation (\"must cut downward\") before the user\ncould open its Heights tab; the only way through was to move G54.\n\nThe fallback is now BottomOfModel+0: a fresh operation's numbers still\nshow where the material is (the intent of the old default), whatever\nthe shop's work-offset convention. fresh_depth_operations_default_to_\nthe_part_and_g54 pinned the old default and is updated and renamed.\n\nFixes #214\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
